# spark community.env -- untested, at your own risk. Any license, named; no
# row here has been proven on the line the way models.env and embers.env
# rows are. A row is a pull request: the model, its license, and an
# optional note. Picking one by name (`spark model NAME` / `spark ember
# NAME`) prints the license line and asks before it downloads; `spark
# setup` never offers these.
#
# Row shape: MODEL_<NAME> as models.env (file url bytes sha256 ram_gb),
# plus:
#   MODEL_<NAME>_LICENSE="<spdx or name> <url>"   required
#   MODEL_<NAME>_NOTE="..."                       optional, one line
MODEL_GEMMA3_12B="google_gemma-3-12b-it-Q4_K_M.gguf https://huggingface.co/bartowski/google_gemma-3-12b-it-GGUF/resolve/main/google_gemma-3-12b-it-Q4_K_M.gguf 7300575264 fc57f67efa46d711c346e587cbef7d049e95f3df8db2eb2271153343ef0acc7b 9"
MODEL_GEMMA3_12B_LICENSE="Gemma-Terms-of-Use https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms"
MODEL_GEMMA3_12B_NOTE="not an open-source license -- read the terms before you download"
